From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riched20: a host's default formats may be NULL

ITextHost::TxGetCharFormat and TxGetParaFormat may answer S_OK and give
no format: Excel's cells do. Wine read the NULL pointer as the editor
was made -- Excel crashed as a blank workbook opened. A NULL format is
now taken as none, and the defaults stand.

Gate: test/richtxsrv2-gate.sh (a windowless host that answers so).
Mutant SG_MUTANT_RICHED_HOST_FORMAT_UNCHECKED.
---
--- a/dlls/riched20/para.c
+++ b/dlls/riched20/para.c
@@ -152,7 +152,7 @@
 {
   ME_Context c;
   CHARFORMAT2W cf;
-  const CHARFORMATW *host_cf;
+  const CHARFORMATW *host_cf = NULL;
   LOGFONTW lf;
   HFONT hf;
   ME_TextBuffer *text = editor->pBuffer;
@@ -192,7 +192,13 @@
   style = ME_MakeStyle(&cf);
   text->pDefaultStyle = style;
 
-  if (ITextHost_TxGetCharFormat(editor->texthost, &host_cf) == S_OK)
+  /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 1513): a host may answer S_OK and give no
+   * format (Excel's cells: a NULL read as a blank workbook opened) */
+  if (ITextHost_TxGetCharFormat(editor->texthost, &host_cf) == S_OK
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_RICHED_HOST_FORMAT_UNCHECKED
+      && host_cf
+#endif
+      )
   {
     ZeroMemory(&cf, sizeof(cf));
     cf.cbSize = sizeof(cf);
@@ -967,8 +973,9 @@
     pFmt->sStyle = -1;
     pFmt->bOutlineLevel = TRUE;
 
+    host_fmt = NULL;
     hr = ITextHost_TxGetParaFormat( editor->texthost, (const PARAFORMAT **)&host_fmt );
-    if (SUCCEEDED(hr))
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr) && host_fmt)
     {
         /* Just use the alignment for now */
         if (host_fmt->dwMask & PFM_ALIGNMENT)
